IMPORT prelude

-- Electricity Act 2001 (Singapore) -- who needs an electricity licence (s 6), high and low voltage (s 2), earthworks near
-- electricity cables (ss 79, 80), who may do electrical work (s 82), the offences of Part 10 and their maxima (ss 83 to 89,
-- 92), the penalty for stealing electricity and the meter-tampering presumption (s 87), officers of a body corporate (s 91),
-- composition (s 93) and serious accidents (s 94).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EA2001.txt, with
-- amendments to Act 27 of 2024 (in force 1 July 2025 and 1 September 2025) and Act 37 of 2021 (in force 1 September 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules an electrician, a
-- contractor digging near cables, a building owner or a householder actually meets. Not encoded: the licensing procedure
-- and licence conditions (ss 7 to 20B), tariffs and supply terms (ss 21 to 27), special administration (Part 4), control of
-- designated licensees (Part 4A), rationing (Part 5A), gas procurement (Part 5B), the wholesale market (Part 6), competition
-- (Part 7), the Appeal Panel (Part 8), installation licence conditions and inspections beyond their offences (ss 67 to 78),
-- cable detection licensing (s 81), and anything left to regulations or Authority directions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in earlier rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electricity Act 2001 -- safety, cables and offences`

§§ `2 -- high voltage and low voltage`

-- s 2: "high voltage" means "a voltage exceeding 1000V a.c. or 1500V d.c. between conductors, or 600V a.c. or 900V d.c.
-- between each conductor and Earth"; "low voltage" means "a voltage not exceeding 1000V a.c. or 1500V d.c. between conductors,
-- or 600V a.c. or 900V d.c. between each conductor and Earth".
-- Read literally, a supply that exceeds one limit but not the other meets BOTH definitions. This encoding treats it as high
-- voltage (an inference: the stricter regime governs). See NOTES.md.

DECLARE Current IS ONE OF
    `alternating current`
    `direct current`

GIVEN `the current` IS A Current, `volts between conductors` IS A NUMBER, `volts to earth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the voltage is high voltage` IF
    CONSIDER `the current`
    WHEN `alternating current` THEN `volts between conductors` GREATER THAN 1000 OR `volts to earth` GREATER THAN 600
    WHEN `direct current` THEN `volts between conductors` GREATER THAN 1500 OR `volts to earth` GREATER THAN 900

GIVEN `the current` IS A Current, `volts between conductors` IS A NUMBER, `volts to earth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the voltage is low voltage only` IF
    NOT `the voltage is high voltage` `the current` `volts between conductors` `volts to earth`

§§ `6 -- activities that need an electricity licence`

-- s 6(1): no person may (a) generate, (b) transmit, (c) transmit for a transmission licensee "(other than as an employee of the
-- transmission licensee)", (d) retail, (e) import or export, (f) provide market support services, (g) trade in, or (h) operate,
-- a wholesale electricity market, or (i) carry on an activity the Minister specifies, "unless the person is authorised to do so
-- by an electricity licence granted under section 9 or is exempted under section 8".
-- s 6(1A): the licence requirement "for a person that engages in the generation or transmission of electricity, imports or
-- exports electricity, or trades in any wholesale electricity market, does not apply to the Authority".
-- s 6(2): fine not exceeding $500,000 and, for a continuing offence, $12,500 for every day or part of a day after conviction.

DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `generating electricity`
    `transmitting electricity`
    `transmitting for a transmission licensee as its employee`
    `transmitting for a transmission licensee as a contractor`
    `retailing electricity`
    `importing or exporting electricity`
    `providing market support services`
    `trading in a wholesale electricity market`
    `operating a wholesale electricity market`
    `using electricity at home`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is listed in s 6(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `transmitting for a transmission licensee as its employee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `using electricity at home` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority is relieved of the licence for the activity` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `generating electricity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `transmitting electricity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `importing or exporting electricity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `trading in a wholesale electricity market` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity, `is the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an electricity licence is required` IF
    `the activity is listed in s 6(1)` `the activity`
        AND (NOT (`is the Authority` AND `the Authority is relieved of the licence for the activity` `the activity`))

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity, `is the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds an electricity licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `is exempted under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is an offence under s 6` IF
    `an electricity licence is required` `the activity` `is the Authority`
        AND (NOT `holds an electricity licence`)
        AND (NOT `is exempted under s 8`)

GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under s 6` MEANS
    500000 PLUS 12500 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `79, 80 -- earthworks near electricity cables`

-- s 79(1): no earthworks "within the vicinity of any low voltage electricity cable" of an electricity licensee "unless the person
-- has caused cable detection work to be carried out by a licensed cable detection worker". (3): does not bind the licensee
-- itself. (2): not a bar where the person "has reasonable cause to believe that it is necessary to do so in the interest of
-- public or private safety", but written notice must then be given to the licensee "not more than 7 days after". (5): $10,000
-- or 12 months or both.
-- s 80(1): near a HIGH voltage cable the person must (a) give the licensee "not less than 7 days' written notice", (b) obtain the
-- location information and consult the licensee, and (c) cause licensed cable detection work to be done. (3): the Authority may
-- modify the 7-day period (not encoded). (6), (6A): the same safety and licensee exceptions. (7): $100,000 or 5 years or both.

GIVEN `near a high voltage cable` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the licensee owning the cable` IS A BOOLEAN, `safety emergency` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days of advance written notice` IS A NUMBER, `obtained location and consulted the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `licensed cable detection done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the high voltage earthworks rule is breached` IF
    `near a high voltage cable`
        AND (NOT `is the licensee owning the cable`)
        AND (NOT `safety emergency`)
        AND (`days of advance written notice` LESS THAN 7
             OR (NOT `obtained location and consulted the licensee`)
             OR (NOT `licensed cable detection done`))

GIVEN `near a low voltage cable` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the licensee owning the cable` IS A BOOLEAN, `safety emergency` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `licensed cable detection done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the low voltage earthworks rule is breached` IF
    `near a low voltage cable`
        AND (NOT `is the licensee owning the cable`)
        AND (NOT `safety emergency`)
        AND (NOT `licensed cable detection done`)

-- s 79(2), 80(6): after emergency earthworks, written notice to the licensee "not more than 7 days after the earthworks have been
-- commenced or carried out". Whether a late notice is itself an offence is not said: s 79(5) and 80(7) punish contraventions of
-- s 79(1) and s 80(1). Encoded only as whether the notice was in time.
GIVEN `days after commencement notice was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the emergency notice was in time` IF
    `days after commencement notice was given` AT MOST 7

-- s 80(9): a defence to s 80(7) "for the person charged to prove" (a) all reasonable steps to discharge the duty or (b) all
-- reasonable precautions and all due diligence. s 80(10): if the defence involves acting on information supplied by the
-- licensee, an infrastructure owner, or a licensed cable detection worker, the person may not rely on it "without permission
-- of the court" unless, "within 14 clear days before the hearing", written notice identifying the supplier was served on the
-- prosecutor. The words "within 14 clear days before" are read here as at least 14 clear days before (an inference).
GIVEN `proved reasonable steps or due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN, `relies on information from licensee or detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `served notice on the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN, `clear days before the hearing` IS A NUMBER, `court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 80(9) defence is available` IF
    `proved reasonable steps or due diligence`
        AND ((NOT `relies on information from licensee or detection worker`)
             OR `court gave permission`
             OR (`served notice on the prosecutor` AND `clear days before the hearing` AT LEAST 14))

§§ `82 -- who may do electrical work`

-- s 82(1): an individual must not carry out electrical work unless "(a) the individual is a licensed electrical worker; or (b) the
-- individual acts under the supervision of an individual who is a licensed electrical worker". (5): an owner or occupier "must not
-- knowingly engage" a person not permitted under (1) or (3). (7): contravention is an offence (no penalty stated: s 92 applies).
-- s 82(8): "it is not unlawful for" (a) a person to replace a lamp in the person's own installation; (b) to replace a fuse in the
-- person's own installation "similar to that of a household"; (c) an officer or employee of the Authority in the course of duty;
-- (e) a non-electrician whose trade includes work on appliances, "so long as the person does not carry out work on any part or
-- circuit which is, or may be, connected to a source of electricity supply"; (f) "a trained person" following the written
-- instructions of the licensed electrical worker in charge.

DECLARE ElectricalTask IS ONE OF
    `replacing a lamp in one's own installation`
    `replacing a household-type fuse in one's own installation`
    `replacing a lamp in a neighbour's installation`
    `adding a power socket in one's own home`
    `rewiring a distribution board`
    `an Authority employee working in the course of duty`
    `an appliance technician repairing a disconnected appliance`
    `an appliance technician working on a circuit connected to supply`
    `a trained employee following the written instructions of the electrical worker in charge`

GIVEN `the task` IS A ElectricalTask
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the task is saved by s 82(8)` IF
    CONSIDER `the task`
    WHEN `replacing a lamp in one's own installation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `replacing a household-type fuse in one's own installation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Authority employee working in the course of duty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an appliance technician repairing a disconnected appliance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a trained employee following the written instructions of the electrical worker in charge` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the task` IS A ElectricalTask, `is a licensed electrical worker` IS A BOOLEAN, `supervised by a licensed electrical worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual may do the work` IF
    `is a licensed electrical worker` OR `supervised by a licensed electrical worker` OR `the task is saved by s 82(8)` `the task`

GIVEN `knew the person was not permitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person engaged was permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner or occupier commits an offence under s 82(5)` IF
    `knew the person was not permitted` AND (NOT `the person engaged was permitted`)

§§ `83 to 89, 92 -- offences and their maxima`

-- Each maximum below is read from the section named. s 92: an offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" carries a fine
-- not exceeding $10,000 or 12 months or both and, for a continuing offence, $250 a day. s 83(2) provides imprisonment up to 5
-- years and no fine. s 6(2) provides a fine and no imprisonment.

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 6 unlicensed activity`
    `s 72 installation not controlled by the directed electrical worker`
    `s 79 earthworks near a low voltage cable without cable detection`
    `s 80(7) earthworks near a high voltage cable in breach`
    `s 80(8) unlicensed cable detection near a high voltage cable`
    `s 82 unlicensed electrical work`
    `s 83(1) supplying electricity without an installation licence`
    `s 83(2) tampering with an installation endangering life`
    `s 83(3) rash or negligent act causing hurt`
    `s 83(4) operating an installation without a licence`
    `s 84 restoring a cut-off supply without consent`
    `s 85 damaging transmission plant or cable`
    `s 85A damaging a submarine cable`
    `s 86 pretending to be a licensee employee to gain entry`
    `s 88 obstructing a licensee employee`
    `s 89 false statement to the Authority`
    `s 94 failing to report a serious accident`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 6 unlicensed activity` THEN 500000
    WHEN `s 80(7) earthworks near a high voltage cable in breach` THEN 100000
    WHEN `s 83(1) supplying electricity without an installation licence` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 83(2) tampering with an installation endangering life` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 85 damaging transmission plant or cable` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `s 85A damaging a submarine cable` THEN 2000000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 6 unlicensed activity` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 80(7) earthworks near a high voltage cable in breach` THEN 60
    WHEN `s 83(1) supplying electricity without an installation licence` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 83(2) tampering with an installation endangering life` THEN 60
    WHEN `s 83(3) rash or negligent act causing hurt` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 83(4) operating an installation without a licence` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 84 restoring a cut-off supply without consent` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 85 damaging transmission plant or cable` THEN 60
    WHEN `s 85A damaging a submarine cable` THEN 60
    OTHERWISE 12

-- Further fine per day (or part of a day) of a continuing offence after conviction. ss 79, 80, 83(1), (2), (3), 85 and 85A
-- state none.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 6 unlicensed activity` THEN 12500
    WHEN `s 79 earthworks near a low voltage cable without cable detection` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 80(7) earthworks near a high voltage cable in breach` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 80(8) unlicensed cable detection near a high voltage cable` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 83(1) supplying electricity without an installation licence` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 83(2) tampering with an installation endangering life` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 83(3) rash or negligent act causing hurt` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 85 damaging transmission plant or cable` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 85A damaging a submarine cable` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 250

§§ `87 -- unauthorised use of electricity`

-- s 87(2): a fine that is the total of "(i) an amount not exceeding $50,000; and (ii) an amount equal to 3 times the value of
-- electricity" abstracted or supplied; imprisonment not exceeding 3 years; and $250 a day for a continuing offence.
GIVEN `value of the electricity` IS A NUMBER, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unauthorised use of electricity` MEANS
    50000 PLUS 3 TIMES `value of the electricity` PLUS 250 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

-- s 87(4): on a charge of meter tampering, if it is proved that at the time (i) a device or wire was attached to or near the meter
-- to alter its index or stop it registering; (ii) the cover had a hole "not a result of ordinary wear and tear"; (iii) a licensee's
-- seal was damaged, removed or changed; (iv) a licensee's paint or chemical on a screw or mechanism was damaged, removed or
-- altered; or (v) a test link was moved; AND (b) the person had custody or control of the meter, the person "is presumed, until the
-- contrary is proved", to have tampered.

DECLARE MeterSign IS ONE OF
    `a device or wire attached to alter the meter`
    `a hole in the cover not from wear and tear`
    `a hole in the cover from ordinary wear and tear`
    `a licensee seal damaged, removed or changed`
    `licensee paint on a screw damaged or removed`
    `a test link position changed`
    `an unusually low bill`

GIVEN `the sign` IS A MeterSign
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sign is listed in s 87(4)(a)` IF
    CONSIDER `the sign`
    WHEN `a hole in the cover from ordinary wear and tear` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an unusually low bill` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the sign` IS A MeterSign, `had custody or control of the meter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `tampering is presumed` IF
    `the sign is listed in s 87(4)(a)` `the sign` AND `had custody or control of the meter`

§§ `91 -- officers of a body corporate`

-- s 91: a director, manager, secretary, similar officer or partner (or one purporting to act as such) is guilty of the body's
-- offence "unless the person proves that (a) the offence was committed without the person's consent or connivance; and (b) the
-- person had exercised all such due diligence". Both limbs must be proved.
GIVEN `was an officer at the time` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty of the body's offence` IF
    `was an officer at the time` AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))

§§ `93 -- composition`

-- s 93(1): the Authority may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding $3,000".
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum` AT MOST 3000

§§ `94 -- serious accidents`

-- s 94(1): where an accident "causing or resulting in loss of life or hurt to any person or serious damage to property" occurs in
-- connection with an installation, the owner of the premises and the Part 9 licensee must report it "by the quickest means
-- available" and then in writing.
GIVEN `loss of life` IS A BOOLEAN, `hurt to a person` IS A BOOLEAN, `serious damage to property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accident must be reported` IF
    `loss of life` OR `hurt to a person` OR `serious damage to property`

-- s 94(3): on "loss of life or grievous hurt", no alteration to the installation or the site "without the approval of the
-- Authority ... until investigations have been completed". (4): "Nothing in subsection (3) operates to interfere with rescue work
-- or other work necessary for the general safety of life or property". Mere hurt or property damage does not freeze the site.
GIVEN `loss of life` IS A BOOLEAN, `grievous hurt` IS A BOOLEAN, `investigations completed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `rescue or safety work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `altering the accident site is forbidden` IF
    (`loss of life` OR `grievous hurt`)
        AND (NOT `investigations completed`)
        AND (NOT `Authority approved`)
        AND (NOT `rescue or safety work`)

-- s 94(5): the Authority "must hold an inquiry" if (a) there is reason to believe the accident was due to failure to comply with
-- the Act or to obey a lawful order, or (b) the investigating officer is satisfied it "might have been prevented if proper
-- precautions had been taken". s 94(2)(e): findings go to the Public Prosecutor if there was loss of life or reason to believe of
-- serious injury.
GIVEN `reason to believe of non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN, `officer satisfied it was preventable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an inquiry must be held` IF
    `reason to believe of non-compliance` OR `officer satisfied it was preventable`

GIVEN `loss of life` IS A BOOLEAN, `reason to believe of serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `preliminary findings go to the Public Prosecutor` IF
    `loss of life` OR `reason to believe of serious injury`
